 ## Overview
-GRay Optimization Settings define the hyperparameter configurations for training 3D Gaussian Splatting using the GRay ray-tracing renderer [S1]. Unlike standard 3DGS or 3DGRT, these settings explicitly disable opacity resets and size-based pruning [S1]. The method offers two distinct presets: **GRayLQ** for high-speed, low-quality training, and **GRayHQ** for high-quality, slower training [S1].
+GRay Optimization Settings define the hyperparameter configurations for training 3D Gaussian Splatting using the GRay ray-tracing renderer [S1]. Unlike standard 3DGS and 3DGRT, GRay does not use opacity resets and does not prune Gaussians based on size [S1]. The settings control the trade-off between training speed, final frame rate, and reconstruction quality through alpha thresholds, pruning thresholds, and spherical harmonic stepping laziness.
 
 ## How it works
-The optimization process manages the set of 3D Gaussians $\mathcal{G}$ by adjusting opacity thresholds, pruning criteria, and spherical harmonic (SH) update frequencies based on the selected preset [S1].
+The optimization process manages Gaussian populations and rendering parameters via specific thresholds and decay rates.
 
